# Milestone: M5
# Covers: at (mytag.enter?) — tier-2 tag-enter event; subscriber fires when
#         OP_PUSH_TAG executes for `mytag`; lazy-alloc of UTag.enter_event on
#         first subscription (spec #3 §3.1).
#
# defer-to: T55 (tag enter/leave emit hooks) + T59 (Tag.new() stdlib)
#
# Reason:
#   Tag.new() requires T59 stdlib binding.  The tier-2 enter/leave event
#   lazy-alloc and OP_PUSH_TAG emit path (T55) are tested by
#   test_tag_enter_leave.c at the C level.  The at (mytag.enter?) subscribe
#   watcher requires OP_AT_EVENT_INSTALL with a tag-event UEvent source;
#   the subscriber body requires scratch-frame execution.
#
# Activate when Tag.new() + enter-event wiring + body dispatch are complete.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at T55 + T59 + M5-scratch-frame):
#   var t = Tag.new("scope");
#   var log = "";
#   at (t.enter?) Realm.log = Realm.log + "in";
#   t: { 1 };
#   log
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000000] nil
#   [00000001] ""
#   [00000002] nil
#   [00000003] 1
#   [00000004] "in"
